<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">John F. Kennedy</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1917">1917</a>–<a href="/years/1963">1963</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as JFK, John Fitzgerald Kennedy</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">John F. Kennedy was the thirty-fifth president of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>, serving from 1961 until his assassination in Dallas in November 1963. A naval officer in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a> and later a congressman and senator from Massachusetts, he was the youngest man elected president and the first Roman Catholic. His administration faced the failed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bay-of-pigs-invasion">Bay of Pigs invasion</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berlin">Berlin</a> crisis and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cuban-missile-crisis">Cuban Missile Crisis</a> of 1962, launched the programme to land astronauts on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhu">Moon</a>, and proposed the civil rights legislation passed after his death.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/john-f-kennedy.jpg" alt="John F. Kennedy" width="320" height="415" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Cecil W. Stoughton · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:John_F._Kennedy,_White_House_color_photo_portrait.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
